# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
# Permutation 2: the same Alloy k8s-monitoring deployment with podLogsViaOpenTelemetry, so
# pod logs leave as OTLP rather than Loki-native. The metrics lane is unchanged, which is the
# point: the disagreement between this and alloy-default is confined to the log transport.
PERMUTATION_TITLE="Alloy k8s-monitoring with podLogsViaOpenTelemetry"
PERMUTATION_SUMMARY="Pod logs leave as OTLP rather than Loki-native; the Prometheus remote-write metrics lane is unchanged."
PERMUTATION_COLLECTOR="grafana/k8s-monitoring"
PERMUTATION_COLLECTOR_VERSION="4.5.0"
PERMUTATION_CORPUS_AREAS="k8s k8s-addons"
PERMUTATION_CAPTURE_STATUS="proven"
PERMUTATION_DEVIATIONS="The capture receiver replaces the hosted Grafana Cloud destinations, so TLS verification is skipped for a throw-away self-signed certificate.|kube-state-metrics is not deployed in this lab, so no kube_* family from that exporter can appear.|profiling, profilesReceiver and autoInstrumentation are off: the capture receiver has no profile route and the BusyBox deck has no eBPF-viable workload."
